1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,429
Coach: A discussion can drift toward an interesting detail

2
00:00:03,429 --> 00:00:05,571
Coach: while leaving its task unfinished.

3
00:00:05,571 --> 00:00:08,143
Coach: Before calling the new topic irrelevant,

4
00:00:08,143 --> 00:00:11,571
Coach: ask what connection it has to the decision.

5
00:00:11,571 --> 00:00:13,286
Coach: Sometimes a detail matters;

6
00:00:13,286 --> 00:00:18,000
Coach: sometimes the group needs to return to a more immediate question.

7
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:22,636
Coach: This is a fresh excerpt from the welcome-activity discussion.

8
00:00:22,636 --> 00:00:26,921
Coach: The group still needs one activity that helps members meet

9
00:00:26,921 --> 00:00:30,350
Coach: and find out about the weekly drawing group.

10
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:32,493
Coach: No activity has been chosen.

11
00:00:32,493 --> 00:00:35,064
Coach: Now a different design question appears.

12
00:00:35,414 --> 00:00:37,985
Noah: The centre's old sign looks dated.

13
00:00:37,985 --> 00:00:40,557
Noah: Which lettering style would be better?

14
00:00:40,907 --> 00:00:43,478
Coach: That question concerns the sign’s appearance.

15
00:00:43,478 --> 00:00:49,479
Coach: We have not yet heard how choosing its lettering would help the welcome activity.

16
00:00:49,479 --> 00:00:52,479
Coach: This is a missing connection to examine,

17
00:00:52,479 --> 00:00:59,336
Coach: not evidence that Noah is careless or that every design question is a waste of time.

18
00:01:07,686 --> 00:01:11,543
You: How would choosing the lettering help new members meet

19
00:01:11,543 --> 00:01:14,543
You: or find out about the drawing group?

20
00:01:14,893 --> 00:01:19,607
Coach: This question gives the idea a chance to earn its place.

21
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:22,607
Coach: A clear link could change your judgement.

22
00:01:22,607 --> 00:01:27,321
Coach: Without that link, the group may spend its discussion comparing styles

23
00:01:27,321 --> 00:01:30,321
Coach: while the required activity is still undefined.

24
00:01:30,321 --> 00:01:34,607
Coach: Keep the task, rather than personal taste, as the reference.

25
00:01:34,957 --> 00:01:40,957
Coach: For example, legibility might matter if an introduction activity uses names written on paper.

26
00:01:40,957 --> 00:01:44,386
Coach: That is a possible task-related design question,

27
00:01:44,386 --> 00:01:47,386
Coach: not a fact about the current proposal.

28
00:01:47,386 --> 00:01:54,243
Coach: Redesigning the centre’s sign is a different issue unless someone explains how it serves this activity.

29
00:01:54,593 --> 00:01:57,593
Coach: Alternatively, if the connection is still unclear,

30
00:01:57,593 --> 00:02:01,450
Coach: suggest returning to an unresolved part of the task.

31
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:06,165
Coach: You do not have to settle every interesting side question now.

32
00:02:06,165 --> 00:02:10,451
Coach: Leave room to reconsider the detail if it becomes useful,

33
00:02:10,451 --> 00:02:13,022
Coach: without promising a separate design project.

34
00:02:13,372 --> 00:02:20,229
You: Could we return to how the welcome activity would connect people with the weekly drawing group?

35
00:02:20,229 --> 00:02:24,086
You: We still need that link before comparing design details.

36
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:28,293
Coach: The return is specific: it names the missing link.

37
00:02:28,293 --> 00:02:33,008
Coach: Simply saying focus, or repeating that the group is off topic,

38
00:02:33,008 --> 00:02:36,436
Coach: gives less help about what to do next.

39
00:02:36,436 --> 00:02:41,151
Coach: A useful redirection makes the task easier to pick up again

40
00:02:41,151 --> 00:02:43,722
Coach: without deciding the answer for everyone.

41
00:02:44,072 --> 00:02:46,643
Coach: Remember what the twenty minutes means.

42
00:02:46,643 --> 00:02:49,644
Coach: It limits the welcome activity being planned,

43
00:02:49,644 --> 00:02:54,358
Coach: not each person’s turn or the time available for this discussion.

44
00:02:54,358 --> 00:02:59,072
Coach: You can point to an unfinished task without inventing a countdown

45
00:02:59,072 --> 00:03:02,501
Coach: or claiming that the group is already late.

46
00:03:02,851 --> 00:03:06,708
Coach: Return to the moment just after the lettering question,

47
00:03:06,708 --> 00:03:09,708
Coach: with no explanation of its relevance yet.

48
00:03:09,708 --> 00:03:11,851
Coach: Privately choose a next line:

49
00:03:11,851 --> 00:03:17,422
Coach: you might ask for the connection or suggest returning to a particular gap.

50
00:03:17,422 --> 00:03:22,565
Coach: Leave room to hear what follows rather than delivering a final verdict.

51
00:03:34,915 --> 00:03:38,772
Coach: Check whether your line uses the shared goals rather

52
00:03:38,772 --> 00:03:41,344
Coach: than a judgement about the speaker.

53
00:03:41,344 --> 00:03:46,058
Coach: A creative idea may become relevant when its purpose is explained.

54
00:03:46,058 --> 00:03:49,486
Coach: For now, help the group find the connection

55
00:03:49,486 --> 00:03:53,772
Coach: or return to the work it still needs to do.
